          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Johan found a 4-litre tub of ice cream. He stopped when he had eaten half of it.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The next night he again stopped when he had eaten half of what was there.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This went on for five nights in a row.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "How much ice cream was left at the end of each of the five nights?",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Would he ever have finished all the ice cream?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Nights 1–5: $2\\text{ L}$, $1\\text{ L}$, $\\frac12\\text{ L}$, $\\frac14\\text{ L}$, $\\frac18\\text{ L}$. No; each night leaves half of the positive amount remaining.",
      "worked": "Half of the remaining ice cream is left each night.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\text{Night 1}&: 4\\times\\frac12=2\\text{ L}\\\\\n\\text{Night 2}&: 2\\times\\frac12=1\\text{ L}\\\\\n\\text{Night 3}&: 1\\times\\frac12=\\frac12\\text{ L}\\\\\n\\text{Night 4}&: \\frac12\\times\\frac12=\\frac14\\text{ L}\\\\\n\\text{Night 5}&: \\frac14\\times\\frac12=\\frac18\\text{ L}\n\\end{align*}$$\nAfter night $n$, the amount left is $4\\times\\left(\\frac12\\right)^n\\text{ L}$. No; repeated halving always leaves a positive amount, so the ice cream never runs out under this process.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 56
